    "description": "When you are wielding two <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Pistols\" title=\"Pistols\">Pistols</a>, as a <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Standard_Action\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Standard Action\">Standard Action</a> you can make an <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Autofire\" title=\"Autofire\">Autofire</a> attack with one of the <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Pistols\" title=\"Pistols\">Pistols</a> as though the Weapon were set to <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Autofire\" title=\"Autofire\">Autofire</a>, even if the <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Pistol\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Pistol\">Pistol</a> would not normally be capable of <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Autofire\" title=\"Autofire\">Autofire</a>.<br><br>The normal penalties for <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Autofire\" title=\"Autofire\">Autofire</a> still apply to this attack roll, and you may split the number of shots consumed between the two <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Pistols\" title=\"Pistols\">Pistols</a>.",
